--   ExprF`, is not one the front end translates — `Functor` is applied to a *family* of types (`ExprF : Type -> Type`) rather than to a type, and the front end has no higher-kinded types
-- polymorphic, and every call of it in this module is inside a declaration that has no program of its own (`instFunctorExprF`), so no call is left to say what type to compile it at: `mapExprF`
